2) SECTION_NAME_N_DESC
Write EXACTLY TWO sentences total.

Sentence 1 rules
- Must start with: This section is about
- Must include EXACTLY three gains: [gain 1], [gain 2], and [gain 3]
- Must end with ONE practical cause to effect outcome using "so": ... so [real-life outcome].

Sentence 2 rules
- Must start with: These jumps
- Add supportive detail that makes Sentence 1 more descriptive (method, tone, framing, or how it sets the stage).
- Keep it simple and concrete.

Template
This section is about [gain 1], [gain 2], and [gain 3] so [practical outcome]. These jumps [how it works / what it uses] to [bridge into what comes next].


3) SECTION_NAME_N_BENEFIT
Write EXACTLY TWO sentences total.

Sentence 1 rules
- Must start with: The benefit of this section is that you will
- List EXACTLY four benefits, comma-separated, with "and" before the last item.

Sentence 2 rules
- Must start with: Practically,
- Translate the benefits into real-life impact (what becomes easier to do, choose, start, or sustain).
- Keep it grounded and usable.

Template
The benefit of this section is that you will [benefit 1], [benefit 2], [benefit 3], and [benefit 4]. Practically, this [real-life translation of those benefits].


4) SECTION_NAME_N_DESC_BENEFIT
Write EXACTLY FOUR sentences total.
- Sentence 1 and Sentence 2 must match SECTION_NAME_N_DESC exactly (same wording, same punctuation).
- Sentence 3 and Sentence 4 must match SECTION_NAME_N_BENEFIT exactly (same wording, same punctuation).
- Combine into one single paragraph with normal spacing between sentences.

Template
[Copy SECTION_NAME_N_DESC sentence 1] [Copy SECTION_NAME_N_DESC sentence 2] [Copy SECTION_NAME_N_BENEFIT sentence 1] [Copy SECTION_NAME_N_BENEFIT sentence 2]


